cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the unpublished manuscript using the preferred citation."
title: "A pure-state matched-basis information inequality violation in dimension five"
authors:
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Dev D.
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An explicit pure state in local dimension five has quantum mutual information
  2 log 5. For the specified complete six mutually unbiased bases, measured
  identically on both parties, every classical mutual information is log 5.
  Every five-setting selection has score 5 log 5, giving a strict matched-basis
  violation with excess 3 log 5 and ratio 5/2. Prior mixed-state ECQC
  counterexamples receive separate credit. Historical novelty remains provisional.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "A pure-state matched-basis information inequality violation in dimension five"
  authors:
